+# REPORT — REVIEW-GATE-SHOWS-FINDINGS-01
+
+dispatch-6af0cc45 · 2026-08-14 · lane worktree `.claude/worktrees/6af0cc45`
+
+## What changed
+
+`plugins/leadv2/scripts/leadv2-review-run.sh` — the review gate now carries the findings
+themselves, not just their counts. Strictly additive: every pre-existing header line
+(`arms:`, `verified:`, `status:`, `critical:`…`low:`, `reviewer:`, `diff:`) keeps its exact
+text on both terminal write sites, and every exit code (0/6/7/9) is untouched.
+
+- **`.review-findings-render.tsv`** — new sidecar (same dotfile convention as
+  `.review-findings-raw.tsv`/`-dedup.tsv`). Truncated once next to `FINDINGS_RAW`; one row
+  per finding appended inside the existing JSON-build loop (`>>`, subshell-safe), columns
+  `severity file line arm dimension verifier_verdict desc`. Arm attribution comes free from
+  the dedup TSV — nothing new is parsed out of review bodies.
+- **`render_gate_findings()` + helpers** (`_review_gate_clip_desc`,
+  `_review_gate_by_arm_line`, `_review_gate_med_rows`/`_low_rows`, `gate_summary_line`),
+  placed beside `review_floor_ok()`. Pure stdout, no side effects, no exits.
+  - Severity floor Medium; three filtered passes over the TSV (no `sort`).
+  - `by_arm:` tally precedes the block — a silent arm shows `=0`, never invisible absence.
+  - Cap `LEADV2_REVIEW_GATE_MAX_FINDINGS` (default 20) with a mandatory
+    `… N more findings omitted (cap=20) — full list: …/review-findings.json` notice.
+    Low is never a row; it is always accounted by `low: N not shown`.
+  - `desc` sanitisation (R1): CR/LF stripped, whitespace collapsed, leading
+    `status:`/`arms:`/`verified:` token stripped, clipped to
+    `LEADV2_REVIEW_GATE_DESC_CHARS` (default 160) with a visible `…` suffix, every row
+    indented 2 spaces — a model-authored desc cannot forge a `^key:` line.
+  - Parse-failure detection (REVIEW-BODY-PERSIST-01 sibling): `reported>0` (reviewer's own
+    `REVIEW_FINDINGS:` header) with 0 machine-readable rows ⇒ `findings_parse: failed` +
+    `findings: PARSE_FAILURE — … Read the full body: docs/handoff/<task>/review-<arm>.md`.
+    Never conflated with the honest `findings: none`.
+- **Line 1 `summary:`** at both terminal write sites:
+  `summary: <verdict> — <N> finding(s): c critical, h high, m medium, l low; <K> shown below`
+  (on the parse-failure path: `… 0 shown — PARSE FAILURE, see review-<arm>.md`).
+- **Pass path additions:** `verdict: <real verdict>` (so `PASS_WITH_NITS` is no longer
+  flattened into a green `status: pass`) and the previously-missing `critical:`…`low:`
+  counts. `status:` text itself is byte-identical everywhere.
+
+Explicitly unchanged (per design §2.5): verdict logic and the contradiction override, all
+exit codes, the `unreviewed`/`blocked` write sites, `review-findings.json` schema, the
+verifier fan-out, `_blocking_refuted`, the WRITE-RACE NOTE and the tmp+`mv -f` atomic write.
+
+Also changed:
